-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",91,{
[2881]="70059B03\n1\tTalk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb\tDurin stands in Mótsog's Tomb far below Gundabad, trying to decide what is to be done.\n2\tWait for Durin to come to a decision\tDurin stands in Mótsog's Tomb far below Gundabad, trying to decide what is to be done.\n3\tTalk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb\tDurin stands in Mótsog's Tomb far below Gundabad.\n4\tTalk to Mótsog and learn if he will accept Durin's decision\tDurin waits for Mótsog's answer.\n5\tTalk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb\tDurin stands in Mótsog's Tomb.\n",
[2882]="7006B594\n1\tFind the entrance to Ghalbûru in Khûd Zagin\tThe hideout of Ghalbûru is among the rocks south-east of the road through Khûd Zagin.\n2\tTalk to Sirgon in Ghalbûru\tSirgon is at the north-western entrance of Ghalbûru.\n3\tTalk to Rothog in Ghalbûru\tRothog is by the water in Ghalbûru.\n4\tTalk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru\tRahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.\n5\tFind Khôltekh inside the caves of Ghalbûru\tKhôltekh is inside the caves of Ghalbûru. The entrance to the caves is in the heights on the eastern side of Ghalbûru.\n6\tExamine the injured man lying on the bed in the caves of Ghalbûru\tKhôltekh has found an injured man resting in the caves of Ghalbûru.\n7\tTalk to Khôltekh in the caves of Ghalbûru\tKhôltekh is in the caves of Ghalbûru.\n8\tTalk to Babarín, the apothecary in Ghalbûru\tGhalbûru's apothecary Babarín is located outside in the village, beneath her canopy on the island in the middle of the pool.\n9\tCollect hardy plant leaves in Ghalbûru (total: 4)\030Collect riverside reeds in Ghalbûru (total: 6)\tIngredients needed by Babarín can be found throughout Ghalbûru: hardy plant leaves and riverside reeds.\n10\tBring the ingredients you collected to Babarín in Ghalbûru\tBabarín is beneath her canopy on the island in the middle of the pool.\n11\tIt will take some time for Babarín to prepare the soothing poultice. You can wait for it to be ready, or you can speak to your companions throughout Ghalbûru.\t\n12\tTalk to Babarín in Ghalbûru\tBabarín is beneath her canopy on the island in the middle of the pool.\n13\tBring the healing poultice to Sadûkh in the caves of Ghalbûru\tSadûkh is resting in the caves of Ghalbûru. The entrance to the caves is located in the heights on the eastern side of Ghalbûru.\n",
[2883]="70059B04\n1\tClimb the secret stair out of the depths and return to Zul-mazal\tDurin has asked you to climb from the depths and return to Zul-mazal, where you can begin gathering the dwarves for Dwarrowmoot.\n2\tTalk to Bósi, Bróin, or Bori in Zul-mazal\030Talk to Prince Ingór at Maergrind in Máttugard\030Talk to Glóin at the Steepset in Máttugard\030Talk to Imák on the western shore of the lake in Gloomingtarn\tDurin asked you to bring word to a number of dwarves about the upcoming Dwarrowmoot: Bósi, Bróin, or Bori at Zul-mazal. Prince Ingór at Maergrind in Máttugard. Glóin at the Steepset in Máttugard. Imák on the western shore of the lake in Gloomingtarn. These dwarves will select others of their kind to attend the Dwarrowmoot. Time is short!\n3\tMeet up with the dwarves on the south-eastern side of the Thing-fold for Dwarrowmoot\tDurin has called for Dwarrowmoot on the south-eastern side of the Thing-fold, in the Welkin-lofts.\n4\tTalk to Durin at the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts\tDurin is at the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts for Dwarrowmoot, but is disappointed that more dwarves have not already arrived.\n5\tDefeat Orc-kind in the Welkin-lofts (total: 10)\030Defeat Angmarim in the Welkin-lofts (total: 8)\tDurin fears that the foes prowling the Welkin-lofts may have hindered the arrival of his dwarves, and wants you to make the high passes as safe as possible.\n6\tTalk to Durin at the Thing-fold\tYour efforts have enabled more dwarves to arrive for the Dwarrowmoot. Durin is eager to begin.\n",
[2884]="700537B6\n1\tRetrieve weather-stained coffer from Sharkey's Slough\tThe shade of Isildur asked you to retrieve a weather-stained coffer from the encampment of Sharkey's Slough, south-west of Tol Send.\n2\tBring the weather-stained coffer to Tol Send\tThe shade of Isildur is waiting for you to bring the weather-stained coffer to Tol Send.\n3\tTalk to Elrond on Tol Send\tElrond is on Tol Send, the Isle of the Flowers in the Gladden Fields. Elrond examines the weather-stained coffer with some interest.\n4\tTalk to the shade of Isildur\tThe shade of Isildur is pleased that you found the weather-stained coffer and brought it to Tol Send, and now wishes to tell you the tale he promised.\n5\tUse the Memories of the Great Alliance and be transported to Mordor Besieged (Second Age)\tThe Memories of the Great Alliance will allow you to experience the Siege of Barad-dûr at the end of the Second Age, as relayed to you by the shade of Isildur.\n6\tTalk to Ontamo in Díngarth, Mordor Besieged\tOntamo is in Díngarth, chief fortification of the Great Alliance in Mordor Besieged.\n",
[2885]="700537B7\n1\tCollect wood for patching the defences of Díngarth (total: 3)\030Collect stone for patching the defences of Díngarth (total: 3)\030Get resting soldiers at Díngarth moving again (total: 6)\tOntamo asked you to collect wood and stone for patching up the fortifications at Díngarth and to keep resting soldiers from giving Isildur the impression of laziness when he comes to inspect the defences.\n2\tRepair the fortifications at Díngarth (quantity: see journal)\tOntamo has asked you to improve the fortifications at spots in need of repair in and around Díngarth.\n3\tTalk to Ontamo at Díngarth\tOntamo awaits your return in Díngarth.\n4\tDefeat Orcs south of Díngarth (total: 6)\tAn Orc raiding party was seen patrolling south of the encampment of Díngarth, and Ontamo asked you to take care of it before King Isildur arrived for his inspection of the defences. Orcs can be found leaving their encampment of Mokh Shapat, far to the south of Díngarth.\n5\tInvestigate the sound of Orc voices far to the south of Díngarth\tThe guttural voices of Orcs can be heard among the rocks far to the south of Díngarth.\n6\tTalk to Magoldir among the bodies of the slain Orcs\tYou have stumbled upon an Elf surrounded by the bodies of a slain Orc raiding party.\n7\tTalk to Ontamo at Díngarth\tOntamo is at Díngarth, awaiting word of your success against the Orcs.\n",
[2886]="7006B595\n1\tAssure Sadûkh that you will protect him\tIn the caves of Ghalbûru, Sadûkh seeks assurances that you will protect him from his enemies.\n2\tTalk to Sadûkh in the caves of Ghalbûru\tSadûkh is resting in the caves of Ghalbûru.\n3\tTalk to Khôltekh in the caves of Ghalbûru\tKhôltekh is in the caves of Ghalbûru.\n4\tTalk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru\tRahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.\n5\tTravel to the entrance of Jirush, located in the desert to the west\tRahâzi has suggested that you go to the town of Jirush in the desert to the west and see if any of the townsfolk there know Balakhad's location.\n6\tTownsfolk of Jirush can be found throughout the city.\t\n7\tTownsfolk of Jirush can be found throughout the city.\t\n8\tCollect sharp teeth from jackals in Khûd Zagin (total: 6)\tErinesh may know something about Balakhad's location, but he wants you to collect jackal teeth for him before he tells you anything. Jackals can be found throughout Khûd Zagin.\n9\tBring the sharp jackal teeth to Erinesh in Jirush\tErinesh stands in the centre of Jirush.\n10\tTalk to Rahâzi in Jirush\tRahâzi is in the centre of Jirush.\n11\tTalk to Sadûkh in the caves of Ghalbûru\tRahâzi suggested that you return to Sadûkh to tell him what you learned of Balakhad's location before you help her infiltrate the fortress above Jirush. Sadûkh is recovering from his injuries in the caves of Ghalbûru.\n12\tTalk to Corudan outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru\tCorudan is outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru, in the heights on the eastern side of the village.\n13\tGo to the north-eastern entrance of Ghalbûru and look for some sign of Sadûkh\tCorudan asked you to go to the north-eastern entrance of Ghalbûru and look for some sign of Sadûkh.\n14\tGo to the south-western entrance to Ghalbûru and look for some sign of Sadûkh\tCorudan asked you to go to the south-western entrance to Ghalbûru and look for some sign of Sadûkh.\n15\tTalk to Urugal at the south-western entrance to Ghalbûru\tUrugal has beckoned for you to speak with him.\n16\tTalk to Corudan outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru\tCorudan is outside the entrance to the caves of Ghalbûru, located in the heights on the eastern side of the village.\n",
[2887]="70059B16\n1\tTalk to Durin and participate in the Dwarrowmoot\tDurin stands at the Thing-fold, prepared to begin the Dwarrowmoot.\n2\tTalk to Durin before the battle is joined\tDurin stands near the Thing-fold, readying himself and his people for battle.\n",
[2888]="7006B597\n1\tTalk to Sigileth on the western side of Ghalbûru\tSigileth is on the western side of Ghalbûru.\n2\tTalk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru\tRahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.\n3\tTalk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru and infiltrate the fortress above Jirush\tRahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru, waiting to go with you to the fortress above Jirush.\n4\tTalk to Sigileth in the centre of Jirush\tSigileth is in the centre of Jirush.\n5\tReturn to the north-west entrance of Ghalbûru, east of Jirush\tSigileth suggested you return to Ghalbûru, but that you keep the information you learned about Balakhad to yourself.\n6\tTalk to Khôltekh at the north-west entrance to Ghalbûru\tKhôltekh is at the north-west entrance to Ghalbûru, east of Jirush.\n",
[2889]="70059B13\n1\tTalk to Durin and accompany Mótsog to the peak... and to Hrímil Frost-heart\tAt the Thing-fold in the Welkin-lofts, Durin prepares for the battle to come.\n2\tTalk to Durin on the mountain-side\tGorgar has been defeated and Hrímil Frost-heart has fled on injured wings, abandoning the high places to Durin's army. You have achieved victory!\n",
[2890]="700537B9\n1\tTalk to one of Isildur's sons at Díngarth\tOntamo feels insulted by Isildur's decision to send his sons to conduct the inspection of Díngarth's defences, and has asked you to speak with them instead.\n2\tTalk to Vëamacil and complete 'Instance: The Sons of Isildur'\tVëamacil is at Díngarth, waiting to take a meal with you before he conducts the inspection of the encampment's defences.\n3\tTalk to Vëamacil at Díngarth\tThe sons of Isildur have conducted their inspection, and now Vëamacil wishes to speak with you.\n4\tTalk to Tárandil at Díngarth\tTárandil is at Díngarth. Vëamacil has decided that you should come with them to Adambel, but that you should first ask his foster-brother Tárandil what he wants as a present for his birthday.\n5\tTalk to Vëamacil at Díngarth\tVëamacil is waiting to speak to you, now that Tárandil has given you no suggestions for his birthday present.\n6\tCollect trophies from Orcs in Arandor (total: 8)\030Collect trophies from wargs in Arandor (total: 4)\tOrcs and wargs can be found throughout Arandor in Mordor Besieged. Vëamacil asked you to collect trophies from Orcs and wargs to give to Tárandil for a birthday present.\n7\tFind Tárandil at the encampment of Adambel\tTárandil has gone to the primary Gondorian encampment of Adambel. Vëamacil asked you to slay Orcs and wargs and bring trophies of your victories to his foster-brother Tárandil as a birthday present.\n8\tGive the trophies to Tárandil as a birthday present\tTárandil is in the primary Gondorian encampment of Adambel.\n9\tTalk to King Isildur at Adambel\tIsildur is at the Gondorian encampment of Adambel.\n",
[2891]="7006B59A\n1\tTalk to Sigileth in Ghalbûru\tSigileth is by the north-western entrance of Ghalbûru.\n2\tTalk to Khôltekh in Ghalbûru\tKhôltekh is by the north-western entrance of Ghalbûru.\n3\tWave to Corudan in Ghalbûru\tYou should wave to your departing companions, and say your farewells to them. Corudan is by the water in Ghalbûru.\n4\tTalk to Corudan in Ghalbûru\tCorudan is by the water in Ghalbûru.\n5\tWave to Sirgon in Ghalbûru\tYou should wave to your departing companions, and say your farewells to them. Sirgon is by the north-western entrance to Ghalbûru.\n6\tTalk to Sirgon in Ghalbûru\030Talk to Belondor in Ghalbûru\tSirgon and Belondor are by the north-western entrance to Ghalbûru.\n7\tWave to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru\tYou should wave to your departing companions, and say your farewells to them. Rahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.\n8\tTalk to Rahâzi in Ghalbûru\tRahâzi is by the water in Ghalbûru.\n9\tTalk to Sigileth in Ghalbûru\tSigileth is by the north-western entrance to Ghalbûru.\n10\tMeet with Sigileth along the road south-east of Jirush, in Khûd Zagin\tSigileth planned to meet with you along the road south-east of Jirush.\n11\tTalk to Sigileth by the road south-east of Jirush\tSigileth stands by the road south-east of Jirush in Khûd Zagin.\n",
[2892]="70059B12\n1\tTalk to Prince Ingór\030Talk to Glóin\030Talk to Bósi\tThe Gabil'akkâ celebrates its victory in Gundabad.\n2\tTalk to Venko\030Talk to Imák\030Talk to Bori\tThe Gabil'akkâ celebrates its victory in Gundabad.\n3\tTalk to Fastrith\030Talk to Bróin\tThe Gabil'akkâ celebrates its victory in Gundabad.\n4\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer\tThe Gabil'akkâ celebrates its victory in Gundabad.\n5\tFind Mótsog down the slope to the west\tMótsog has stepped away, unnoticed, from the celebrating throng.\n6\tTalk to Mótsog high above Gundabad\tMótsog stands on the slope, watching the setting sun.\n7\tTalk to Durin high above Gundabad\tDurin is up the slope to the east, celebrating the victory of the dwarves.\n",
[2893]="700537D0\n1\tTalk to the shade of Isildur at Adambel\tThe shade of Isildur has interrupted the telling of his tale with a brief aside.\n2\tTalk to Isildur at Adambel\tKing Isildur of Gondor is at the encampment of Adambel.\n3\tFind a crate of whetstones in Adambel\tA crate of whetstones can be found by the camp-fires to the north in Adambel, the primary Gondorian encampment in Mordor Besieged.\n4\tIdle soldiers can be found throughout Adambel. Isildur asked you to deliver whetstones to idle soldiers of the Alliance, as well as to his sons.\t\n5\tDeliver whetstones to idle soldiers and the sons of Isildur (5/6)\tIdle soldiers can be found throughout Adambel. Isildur asked you to deliver whetstones to idle soldiers of the Alliance, as well as to his sons.\n6\tDeliver a whetstone and a warning to High King Elendil at Adambel\tHigh King Elendil can be found somewhere within Adambel, the primary Gondorian encampment in Mordor Besieged.\n7\tHigh King Elendil has commanded that you train with soldiers at the encampment of Adambel and remind them not to relax their guard despite the length of the siege.\t\n8\tTalk to Vëamacil at Adambel\tVëamacil is at Adambel. Now that you have trained with the soldiers, High King Elendil expects you to convey his reprimand to his grandson Vëamacil.\n9\tGive Magoldir a whetstone at Adambel\tMagoldir is at Adambel, the primary Gondorian encampment in Mordor Besieged.\n",
[2894]="700537D2\n1\tFind the location east of Adambel that Magoldir wishes to scout\030Defeat foes of the Great Alliance in Parth Daenath (total: 10)\030Talk to Magoldir on the northern slope of Amon Amarth\tMagoldir desires to scout a location to the east of Adambel for Glorfindel of the Bright Company.\n2\tFind the entrance to Echad-in-Edhil\030Talk to Magoldir at the entrance to Echad-in-Edhil\tMagoldir wishes to report to Glorfindel of the Bright Company at the encampment of Echad-in-Edhil, north-west of Adambel in Mordor Besieged.\n3\tTalk to Magoldir and complete 'Instance: Tales of the Bright Company'\tMagoldir stands at the entrance of Echad-in-Edhil, waiting for your readiness to report to Glorfindel, leader of the Bright Company.\n4\tTalk to Glorfindel at Echad-in-Edhil\tGlorfindel, leader of the Bright Company, is waiting to speak with you in the Elf-camp of Echad-in-Edhil.\n",
[2895]="7006B59B\n1\tFind a side door to one of the tomb annexes in which Balakhâd might hide\030Defeat wights at Nirgambâr (total: 5)\tThe ruins of Nirgambâr may hide the one you seek. Sigileth thinks you should search for a less-grand entrance to the tombs in which Balakhâd might hide. She also wants you to defeat some of the wights that make exploring the ruins dangerous.\n2\tTalk to Sigileth west of Nirgambâr\tSigileth is west of Nirgambâr, in Khûd Zagin.\n3\tUse the entrance to the crypts below south-eastern Nirgambâr\tSigileth is ready to go with you into the crypts of south-eastern Nirgambâr.\n4\tSearch the south-eastern tomb in Nirgambâr for Balakhad's hiding-place\tSigileth believes Balakhad may be hiding somewhere within one of the less-grand tombs of south-eastern Nirgambâr.\n5\tSearch the satchel in the chamber below Nirgambâr\tA satchel lies discarded in the corner deep below Nirgambâr.\n6\tBring the contents of the satchel to Sigileth in the chamber below Nirgambâr\tSigileth is in the chamber below Nirgambâr.\n",
[2896]="700537D7\n1\tGlorfindel asked you to deliver the scouting reports to either Isildur or Anárion at the Gondorian encampment of Adambel.\t\n2\tBring Anárion's message to Martore\030Bring Anárion's message to Tumbomehtar\030Bring Anárion's message to Astondor\030Defeat beasts and servants of Sauron in Mordor Besieged (total: 16)\tAnárion asked you to bring his message to soldiers in the field east of Adambel, nearer to the Dark Tower. He also charged you with defeating servants of Sauron and the beasts that stalk among the crags of Mordor.\n3\tReturn to Anárion at Adambel\tYou have done as Anárion asked, and should return to him at Adambel.\n4\tTalk to Tárandil at Adambel\tAnárion has been summoned to an urgent council and is unavailable. Isildur's foster-son Tárandil has called you over and wishes to speak with you.\n5\tTalk to Vëamacil at Díngarth\tVëamacil is at Díngarth. Tárandil told you that his brothers may have found some clue to the mystery of the missing soldiers.\n",
[2897]="7006B59C\n1\tMeet up with Sigileth far to the south-east at the Oasis of Shonith\tShonith is an oasis far away in south-eastern Khûd Zagin.\n2\tTalk to Sigileth in south-western Shonith\tSigileth is on the leader's rise in the south-western reaches of Shonith.\n3\tTalk to Tharashil at Shonith\tTharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.\n4\tWalk closer to the edge of the overlook and look out over Shonith\tTharashil asked you to look out over Shonith and consider the work of the Kintai.\n5\tTalk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith\tTharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.\n6\tCollect sand-sifter meat in Khûd Zagin (total: 4)\030Collect bird feathers in Khûd Zagin (total: 6)\tSand-sifters and birds can be found throughout the desert regions of Khûd Zagin.\n7\tLeave the meat and feathers in the coffer north of the water in Shonith\tTharashil asked you to leave the meat and feathers you collected in the coffer north of the water in Shonith.\n8\tTalk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith\tTharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.\n9\tTalk to Sigileth at Shonith\tSigileth is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.\n",
[2898]="7006B5AA\n1\tTalk to Tharashil at Shonith\tTharashil has much to tell you about her people, the Kintai.\n2\tTalk to Tharashil at Shonith\tTharashil has much to tell you about her people, the Kintai.\n3\tMeet with Aitárshun on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith\tAitárshun is on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith, reachable by the bridges.\n4\tTalk to Aitárshun in Shonith\tAitárshun is on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith.\n5\tWait for Aitárshun to turn his attention to you\tAitárshun is on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith.\n6\tTalk to Aitárshun in Shonith\tAitárshun is on the easternmost island in the water in Shonith.\n7\tTalk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith\tTharashil is on the leader's rise in south-western Shonith.\n8\tFind Silirtas at Er-atûr, north-west of Shonith\tEr-atûr is to the north-west of Shonith.\n9\tTalk to Sigileth at Er-atûr\tSigileth is at Er-atûr, north-west of Shonith.\n10\tTalk to Silirtas at Er-atûr\tSilirtas is at Er-atûr, north-west of Shonith.\n",
[2899]="700537D8\n1\tTalk to Tûka, leader of the Hól-budlan, on the outskirts of Díngarth\tTûka, leader of the Hól-budlan, may have some clue as to what befell the missing soldiers. She can be found in Díngarth.\n2\tTalk to Ornaher at Díngarth\tIsildur's son Ornaher can be found in Díngarth with the Hól-budlan matriarch Tûka.\n3\tTalk to Vëamacil at Díngarth\tIsildur's son Vëamacil can be found at Díngarth.\n",
[2900]="700537D9\n1\tTalk to Vëamacil and complete 'Instance: All Is Quiet'\tIsildur's son Vëamacil is at Díngarth.\n2\tTalk to Tárandil at Ram Raedas\tIsildur's foster-son Tárandil is at Ram Raedas.\n3\tTalk to Meldaran at Ram Raedas\tIsildur's son Meldaran has come to Ram Raedas with worrying tidings.\n",
[2901]="7006B5D4\n1\tExamine sand in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed\tSilirtas asked you to investigate the dry river-bed where once the River Usâl ran through Khûd Zagin, to the west.\n2\tExamine sand further to the north-west, alongside the little water that remains in the channel of the River Usâl\tSilirtas asked you to investigate the river-bed where once the River Usâl ran through Khûd Zagin. To the north-west you see some water remains in the channel.\n3\tContinue further to the north-west and examine some of the sand among the tumbled rocks\tSilirtas asked you to investigate the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once ran through Khûd Zagin. To the north-west a tumble of stones fills the channel.\n4\tTalk to Silirtas in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed\tSilirtas stands in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed.\n5\tTalk to Sigileth in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed\tSilirtas stands in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed, but she says nothing.\n6\tTalk to Silirtas in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed\tSilirtas stands in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed, but she says nothing.\n7\tTalk to Sigileth in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed\tSigileth is in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed.\n8\tTalk to Silirtas in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed\tSilirtas is in the dry river-bed where the River Usâl once flowed. She again seems aware of both you and Sigileth.\n9\tLizards and avanc can be found in the south-western corner of Khûd Zagin.\t\n10\tLizards and avanc can be found in the south-western corner of Khûd Zagin.\t\n11\tJoin Sigileth and Silirtas in the desert of southern Khûd Zagin\tSigileth has found something among the southern sands of Khûd Zagin.\n12\tTalk to Sigileth in southern Khûd Zagin\tSigileth has found something in southern Khûd Zagin.\n",
[2902]="700135D5\n1\tTalk to Snár the Forge-master at the Forges of Rivendell\tSnár the Forge-master can be found by the Forges of Rivendell. Your weapon possesses hidden potential that can be unlocked by reforging at a Forge-master. This process increases the weapon's damage and reveals a weapon's potential.\n2\tTalk to Dithalion\tDithalion is by the Forges of Rivendell. Now that you have reforged the weapon, you should return to Dithalion to demonstrate its development.\n3\tTalk to Ráthwald\tRáthwald is at the crumbling arch near the camp of Echad Dúnann in Eregion. Your weapon has become powerful indeed, perhaps powerful enough to use in battle with the Watcher before the Doors of Durin.\n",
[2903]="70025395\n1\tTalk to Corunir at Zudrugund\tCorunir is at Zudrugund. Halbarad wants you to tell Corunir to come back to Lhanuch.\n2\tTalk to Nár at Zudrugund\tNár is in Zudrugund. Corunir, angered by the loss of his friends along the Forsaken Road, has forced Frithgeir to give Nár the strange-smelling brew once again, in order for dwarf to give clear answers about his knowledge.\n3\tTalk to Corunir in Zudrugund\tCorunir is at Zudrugund. You have spoken with Nár about a number of topics of interest to Corunir and should tell the Ranger what you have learned.\n",
[2904]="7001B5C5\n1\tTalk to Ningloril at Thangúlhad\tNingloril is in Thangúlhad, east of Ost Galadh, in Gathbúrz. Gruingalas has sent you to offer your aid to Ningloril, now that the errand of the Hidden Guard has failed.\n",
[2905]="70021E90\n1\tTalk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan\tSaeradan is at his camp, Echad Saeradan, in the Windfells, in Enedwaith. His camp can be found on a hilltop in the Windfells, south-west of Echad Dagoras. Lothrandir has sent you into the Windfells to assist Saeradan.\n2\tInvestigate the road north of Echad Saeradan for evidence of a blockade\tThe road north of Echad Saeradan may have been blockaded by forces of Saruman. Saeradan has asked you to investigate the road north for signs of blockade.\n3\tBring the report and the ancient sword to Saeradan\tSaeradan is at his camp south of the blockaded road in Fordirith. You found a report and a sword with ancient markings in the coffer at the blockaded road and should bring them to Saeradan.\n",
[2906]="700135D4\n1\tTalk to Wafi\030Talk to Dithalion\tWafi is in the Forging Hall of Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin, and Dithalion is by the Forges of Rivendell. Now that you have fought many foes with your new weapon, you should return to either Wafi or Dithalion to demonstrate your progress.\n",
[2907]="700539E3\n1\tTalk to Ornaher at Díngarth\tIsildur's son Ornaher is at Díngarth.\n2\tSpeak inspiring words to fearful soldiers at Ram Raedas (0/8)\tFearful soldiers can be found at Díngarth, despairing at the news of the approaching Rhúnhoth horde.\n3\tCollect abandoned weapons at Díngarth (total: 4)\tWords are no more use to the despairing soldiers of the Great Alliance. Better now to collect the weapons they cast aside with the hope that they will still be of use to those who remain to fight.\n4\tDeliver abandoned weapons to Ornaher at Díngarth\tYou have gathered many weapons cast aside by despairing soldiers at Díngarth, and should bring them to Ornaher for distribution to those who may still wield them.\n5\tRemind Men of the Alliance about Narsil, the sword of Elendil (total: 3)\030Remind Elves of the Alliance about Aiglos, the spear of Gil-galad (total: 3)\tFrightened Men and Elves can be found at Díngarth. Ornaher believes tales of Elendil's sword Narsil and Gil-galad's spear Aiglos may inspire the frightened Men and Elves to stand against the Ghâzab Bôron.\n6\tTalk to Tárandil at Díngarth\tTárandil is at Díngarth, and he desires to speak with you.\n",
[2908]="7006B5DC\n1\tCollect a jar front the northern pavilion to fill with water for Balakhâd\030Talk to Idhraid by the northern pavilion\tSilirtas suggested that you speak with Idhraid about what it will take to heal Balakhâd of his injuries, and also that you fill a jar with water from the deepest part of the oasis. Jars for this purpose can be found at the front of the pavilion in northern Shonith.\n2\tDampen the cloth and fill the jar with water from the deepest part of the oasis\tYou should dampen the cloth given to you by Idhraid and fill the jar you collected with water from the deepest reaches of the oasis in Shonith.\n3\tBring the damp cloth and water jar to Silirtas at the northern pavilion in Shonith\tSilirtas is waiting for you to return to her with the damp cloth and water jar she requested of you.\n4\tWait for Silirtas to soothe Balakhâd's burning skin with the damp cloth\tSilirtas has begun trying to ease Balakhâd's hurts with the damp cloth.\n5\tHelp Balakhâd drink from the jar of water\tBalakhâd is at the northern pavilion in Shonith.\n6\tTalk to Sigileth at the northern pavilion in Shonith\tSigileth is at the northern pavilion in Shonith.\n7\tTalk to Tharashil in south-western Shonith\tTharashil is in south-western Shonith.\n",
[2909]="700539E5\n1\tCollect a badge from a hopeful Orc patrol-leader\030Collect a badge from a Mordorrim hopeful\030Collect a badge from an Easterling hopeful\tPatrol leaders, and others who intend to lead such excursions, can be found throughout Parth Daenath. Mordorrim hopefuls gather west of the entrance to Amon Fuin, and hopeful Orcs can be found in and around Mokh Darga. Look for Easterling hopefuls south of the road halfway between Mokh Darga and Barthost. Tárandil believes that proof of your value to the Great Alliance will gain the two of you entrance to the council of the kings, and he wants you to collect badges of rank belonging to hopeful patrol leaders as proof of that value.\n2\tBring the patrol badges to Tárandil at Adambel\tTárandil is at Adambel, hoping to attend the council of the kings.\n3\tTalk to Tárandil and complete 'Instance: The Council of Kings'\tTárandil is at Adambel, hoping to attend the council of the kings.\n4\tTalk to Vëamacil at Adambel\tVëamacil is at Adambel, dismayed by the result of the council of the kings.\n5\tTalk to Elendil at Adambel\tHigh King Elendil is at Adambel, and has asked to speak with you.\n",
[2910]="7006B5F1\n1\tCross the River Barûg into Imhûlar from Khûd Zagin, north of Shonith\tThe road into Imhûlar crosses the River Barûg north of Shonith.\n2\tTalk to Sigileth by the road into Imhûlar\tSigileth stands just within the entrance to Imhûlar.\n3\tTalk to Silirtas by the road into Imhûlar\tSilirtas is just inside the entrance to Imhûlar.\n4\tCollect diseased boar-hooves (total: 4)\030Collect diseased serval-fangs (total: 4)\030Collect diseased deer-hides (total: 4)\tDiseased boars, servals, and deer can be found throughout Imhûlar.\n5\tFind Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin, in southern Imhûlar\tThe leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin is named Thórvilon, and can be found in southern Imhûlar.\n6\tTalk to Thórvilon in Vartúlin\tThórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin, is in southern Imhûlar.\n7\tTalk to Silirtas in Vartúlin\tSilirtas stands by Thórvilon in Vartúlin.\n8\tGive the hooves, fangs, and hides to Thórvilon\tThórvilon, leader of the Kintai at Vartúlin is in southern Imhûlar.\n",
[2911]="700539EB\n1\tFind Tûka outside the entrance to the tunnel of Halroth\tTûka is outside the tunnel of Halroth, which the Bright Company hopes to use to infiltrate Barad-dûr.\n2\tTalk to Tûka outside the entrance to Halroth\tTûka is outside the entrance of Halroth, a tunnel carved in the rocks of Mordor.\n3\tDefeat just the right number of enemies outside Halroth, in Emyn Duir\tDefeat enemies in the vicinity of the entrance to the tunnel of Halroth, in Emyn Duir. Tûka thinks you should defeat watchful eyes near the entrance to Halroth, not too many and not too few.\n4\tDefeat just the right number of enemies outside Halroth, in Emyn Duir\tDefeat enemies in the vicinity of the entrance to the tunnel of Halroth, in Emyn Duir. Tûka thinks you should defeat watchful eyes near the entrance to Halroth, not too many and not too few.\n5\tTalk to Tûka outside the entrance to Halroth\tTûka is outside the entrance of Halroth, a tunnel carved in the rocks of Mordor.\n6\tTalk to Vëamacil at Adambel\tVëamacil is at Adambel, and he wishes to speak with you.\n7\tTalk to Vëamacil and complete 'Instance: A Bad Birthday'\tVëamacil is at Adambel, and he wishes to speak with you.\n8\tTalk to the shade of Isildur on Tol Send\tThe shade of Isildur is on Tol Send, waiting to tell you more of the tale of the Great Alliance.\n9\tTalk to Glorfindel on Tol Send\tGlorfindel is on Tol Send. Glorfindel has interrupted the shade of Isildur in his telling of the tale, and wishes to speak with you.\n10\tTalk to Gandalf on Tol Send\tGandalf is on Tol Send. He has listened with interest to the tale told by the shade of Isildur, but does not understand the need for Glorfindel's interruption.\n11\tTalk to Glorfindel on Tol Send\tGlorfindel is on Tol Send, and he has volunteered to complete the tale begun by the shade of Isildur, despite his misgivings.\n",
[2912]="7006B5F2\n1\tPick up boundary stones from the pile across the bridge in Vartúlin\tA pile of the boundary stones can be found across the bridge in Vartúlin.\n2\tPlace a boundary stone north of Thórvilon\030Place a boundary stone at the north-eastern entrance to Vartúlin\030Place a boundary stone on the slope to the southern pavilion in Vartúlin\030Place a boundary stone at the western entrance to Vartúlin\tThórvilon has asked you to place boundary stones around the edges of Vartúlin.\n3\tTalk to Silirtas in the centre of Vartúlin\tThat should be enough stones to fulfil Thórvilon's request.\n4\tTalk to Silirtas in the centre of Vartúlin\tHaving satisfied Thórvilon's request, you should return to the centre of Vartúlin and check on Silirtas.\n5\tTalk to Sigileth in Vartúlin\tSigileth is in Vartúlin.\n6\tTravel toward Kûr Anzar, to the north of Vartúlin\tSigileth wants to rejoin the rest of your travelling company at Kûr Anzar, to the north of Vartúlin.\n7\tDefeat wights near Adakûr in Imhûlar (total: 8)\tYou should defeat some of the Dead that lurk at Adakûr before they threaten the folk that live in Imhûlar.\n8\tTalk to Sigileth outside Adakûr\tSigileth is outside Adakûr in Imhûlar.\n9\tLook at Kûr Anzar from here\030Find the location to the north-east from which to look at Kûr Anzar\tSigileth wants you to look at Kûr Anzar from a location to the north-east and determine the situation inside the city.\n10\tTalk to Sigileth outside Adakûr\tSigileth is outside Adakûr in Imhûlar.\n",
})
